## Overflow menus (3-dot)

**ALWAYS** use the Contracts table trigger (`ActionDropdown`). Do **not** use Lucide `MoreVertical` / `EllipsisVertical` for row or card overflow menus.

```tsx
<DropdownMenu>
  <DropdownMenuTrigger
    className="shad-no-focus rounded-full transition-colors hover:bg-white/30"
    aria-label={`Actions for ${itemName}`}
  >
    <Image src="/assets/icons/dots.svg" alt="" width={34} height={34} />
  </DropdownMenuTrigger>
  <AppDropdownMenuContent align="end">
    <AppDropdownMenuItem icon={Pencil} onClick={...}>
      Edit
    </AppDropdownMenuItem>
    <DropdownMenuSeparator />
    <AppDropdownMenuItem icon={Trash2} tone="danger" onClick={...}>
      Delete
    </AppDropdownMenuItem>
  </AppDropdownMenuContent>
</DropdownMenu>
```

**Required:**
- Icon: `/assets/icons/dots.svg` at `width={34}` `height={34}`
- Trigger: `shad-no-focus rounded-full transition-colors hover:bg-white/30`
- Items: `AppDropdownMenuItem` with a Lucide `icon` (and `tone="danger"` for delete/archive)
- `aria-label` on the trigger that names the row (`Actions for {title}`)

**Delete / Archive divider (required):** If the menu includes Delete, Archive, or any other destructive item, put `<DropdownMenuSeparator />` immediately **above** that item. Never sit a destructive action flush against Edit / History / other safe actions.

**Reference:** `src/components/ActionDropdown.tsx` (contracts table), `src/components/licenses/LicenseActionDropdown.tsx`

