## Badges

**ALWAYS** use the CAALM badge pattern from the Contracts table. Do **not** use unstyled shadcn `Badge` variants (`default`, `secondary`, `outline`, `destructive`) as the final look.

```tsx
<span className="inline-block px-2 py-0.5 text-xs rounded-full font-medium border bg-green/10 text-green border-green/20">
  Active
</span>
```

**Shape (required):** `inline-block px-2 py-0.5 text-xs rounded-full font-medium border`

**Status / meaning colors (required):**

| Meaning | Classes |
|---|---|
| Success / active / current | `bg-green/10 text-green border-green/20` |
| Warning / pending / draft | `bg-orange/10 text-orange border-orange/20` |
| Danger / expired / action required | `bg-red/10 text-red border-red/20` |
| Info / category / in progress | `bg-blue/10 text-blue border-blue/20` |
| Neutral / inactive / version | `bg-slate-100 text-slate-600 border-slate-200` |

**Rules:**
- Use custom colors with opacity (`bg-green/10`), never `bg-green-100` / `bg-blue-100`
- Capitalize labels (`Active`, `Draft`), do not dump raw enum strings (`active`)
- `Badge` from `@/components/ui/badge` is allowed only when these classes override the default variant (see department tables). Prefer a `<span>` like `ContractsTableView`

**Reference:** `src/components/ContractsTableView.tsx` (`statusBadge`), `src/components/Card.tsx`, `src/components/licenses/LicenseCard.tsx`

