## Interactive glass cards

Use **static** glass for display-only content. Use **interactive** glass when the whole card is clickable.

### Static (display only)

```tsx
<Card className="glass-card">
  <div className="glass-card-cap" />
  <CardContent className="p-4 sm:p-6">{/* content */}</CardContent>
</Card>
```

### Interactive (clickable)

```tsx
<Card className="glass-card interactive-glass-card" tabIndex={0} role="button" onClick={...}>
  <div className="glass-card-cap" />
  <CardContent className="p-4 sm:p-6">{/* content */}</CardContent>
</Card>
```

Or combine: `className="glass-card interactive-glass-card"`.

**Rules:**
- `cursor-pointer` on all clickable cards, rows, and icon buttons
- Hover via color/border/shadow only — no `scale-*` that shifts layout
- `transition-all duration-200` on interactive glass
- `focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-[#0f5384]/40` for keyboard users

---

## Glass contrast rules

| Surface | Minimum fill | Text |
|---------|--------------|------|
| `.glass-card` | `rgba(255,255,255,0.55)` | `text-slate-700` body, `text-slate-600` muted |
| `.glass-card-inner` | `rgba(255,255,255,0.30)` | Same as above |
| `.glass-card-frosted` | `rgba(255,255,255,0.55)` | Dialog content on `bg-slate-50` |

Never use `bg-white/10` for primary readable content. Ensure 4.5:1 contrast on light backgrounds.

